  <section aria-labelledby="faq-title">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 id="faq-title">Short answers</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Is DHUN only a YouTube Music client?</h3>
        <p>No. DHUN is a multi-source music client by direction, with YouTube /
        YouTube Music first priority. Native builds currently use that source;
        browser uses JioSaavn through unofficial wrappers. Spotify is planned,
        not implemented, and deferred pending technical, account/Premium, policy,
        legal, playback, privacy and cost gates. Other sources need evidence-based
        evaluation; capabilities may differ by platform.</p>
        <!-- docs/PRD.md §1; docs/research/05-source-capability-matrix.md; ADR-010 -->
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Does DHUN need a YouTube Music account?</h3>
        <p>No provider sign-in is implemented in the current native YouTube Music
        path. It uses guest requests and session visitor identifiers, not imported
        cookies or PO tokens. This is not anonymity or a guarantee of playback;
        future providers may require accounts.</p>
        <!--ADR-001, ADR-003 -->
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Does it work offline?</h3>
        <p>Native Android/desktop code can play completed downloads from local
        storage. Native streaming also uses a bounded Android segment cache or
        desktop whole-track/LRU cache and prebuffer; artwork and lyrics can be
        cached too. Persistent downloads are separate from those caches. Provider
        permission for downloading/caching remains unresolved. Browser offline
        support is the interface and local library display only, not offline music.</p>
        <!--ADR-006 -->
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>What does it cost, and how is it funded?</h3>
        <p>DHUN software is free and GPL-3.0, with no paid DHUN tier,
        advertising SDK or telemetry. Current hosting uses GitHub. Planned
        providers may require accounts/subscriptions or approval; no new paid
        or recurring service is authorised. Software licences do not grant
        third-party music or API rights.</p>
        <!--LICENSE; THIRD_PARTY.md -->
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>What does the Android build ask for?</h3>
        <p>{{ site.install.permissions }}</p>
        <!--{{ site.install.source }}-->
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>What does it send anywhere?</h3>
        <p>No DHUN telemetry SDK is present, but using the app sends provider
        requests: native queries/IDs and visitor identifiers to YouTube/Google,
        track metadata to configured LRCLIB/KuGou lyrics services, or browser
        queries/IDs to JioSaavn wrappers and media/artwork to its CDN. GitHub hosts
        the site. Local library storage is not a promise that nothing leaves your
        device. Spotify has no active requests. See the build-specific Privacy drafts.</p>
        <!--{{ site.install.sourceTwo }}-->
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Which platforms actually work?</h3>
        <p>Android 7.0+ and Windows are the primary native targets, with hardware
        acceptance gates still open; desktop playback needs system VLC. Linux/macOS
        JVM builds remain hardware-unverified. The separate browser client is
        experimental JioSaavn, with live catalogue access and audible playback from
        the deployed origin unverified. Compilation and unit tests do not prove audio.</p>
        <!--MASTER_PROMPT §1; S3 checklists -->
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

